The following files are part of this release of TIGER 2.2.doc:

* authors.tsv --	table of tab-separated values,
					first column: DocumentID,
					second column: author's name,
					third column: author's gender,
					fourth column: second author's name (if exists),
					fifth column: second author's gender (if exists),
					sixth column: third author's name (if exists),
					seventh column: third author's gender (if exists),
					NOTE: rows ordered by DocumentID

* documents.tsv --	table of tab-separated values,
					first column: DocumentID,
					second column: sentence number,
					NOTE: rows ordered by sentence number

* documents_notes.tsv --	table of tab-separated values,
						first column: DocumentID,
						second column: category of note (COLLECTION, OTHER),
						third column:
							for category COLLECTION: type/heading of COLLECTION document,
							for category OTHER: description,
						NOTE: rows ordered by DocumentID
											
* documents_train.tsv --	list of DocumentIDs for the training part of the treebank					
* documents_dev.tsv --	list of DocumentIDs for the development part of the treebank
* documents_test.tsv --	list of DocumentIDs for the test part of the treebank

* origin_md.tsv --	table of tab-separated values,
					first column: OriginID,
					second column: short metadata string,
					thrid column: long metadata string,
					NOTE: rows ordered by OriginID,
					Origin metadata taken from Negra export format of TIGER Corpus 1,
					TIGER Corpus 2.1 and an old work file

* README -- this file

* sentences.tsv --	table of tab-separated values,
					first column: DocumentID,
					second column: sentence number,
					third column: sentence type (Header, Body, Meta, --),
					NOTE: sentences from documents of type COLLECTION are not annotated with types and received '--',
					rows ordered by DocumentID
					
NOTE: Documents of type COLLECTION contain several short but independent news features in one document.

Read about this dataset in: 
Falenska, A. and Eckart, K. and Kuhn, J. (2018). Moving TIGER beyond Sentence-Level. Proceedings of the Eleventh International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation (LREC 2018), Miyazaki, Japan.